# Agent Doc Maintenance

When a change makes agent docs **wrong or incomplete**, update them **in the same task** — not a follow-up.

## Triggers — update docs when you…

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| Add/rename/remove screen, route, or tab | `AGENTS.md`, `react-native-expo.mdc`, relevant skill |
| Add/rename/remove component | `DESIGN.md` catalog, relevant skill |
| Change board/chess rendering | `DESIGN.md` § Chess, `chess-board.mdc`, `chess-ui` skill |
| Add package, API route, or table | `AGENTS.md` structure, `backend-api.mdc` or domain rule |
| New convention or constraint | matching `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` + `AGENTS.md` constraints |
| Stitch re-sync | `DESIGN.md`, `tokens.ts`, `stitch-designs` skill |
| New skill-worthy workflow | `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`; list in `AGENTS.md` |
| Mobile routes or onboarding flow | `ios-simulator-testing` skill P0 scenarios |
| New interactives without a11y labels | `design-system.mdc`, `ios-simulator-testing.mdc` |
| Rule scope no longer matches paths | rule frontmatter `globs` |

## Do not

- Leave docs describing removed files, screens, or APIs
- Add code that contradicts rules without updating the rule
- Defer doc fixes to "later"

## How

1. Finish the code change
2. Grep docs for stale names/paths (`AGENTS.md`, `DESIGN.md`, `.cursor/`)
3. Patch only affected sections — keep rules under ~50 lines
4. If `AGENTS.md` rules/skills tables changed, verify both tables match disk

Skill: `.cursor/skills/doc-maintenance/SKILL.md`
